  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Teenz Alliance in Ending Sexual Violence in Schools</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">People Opposing Women Abuse (POWA) and ADAPT will work in 12 schools in two districts in Gauteng Province, Tembisa and Evaton. They will develop schools based activities including girls Teenz leadership clubs, activities to promote safety across the school led by learners, campaigns on specific issues, and regular community dialogues. They will also work to address male attitudes to girls and towards sexual violence.</narrative>
  </description>
